", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That made `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` fail, because 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986), `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 with the advisory tool to confirm the requirement, but it doesn't know that ID, so it's probably an internal ticket. The change follows the test and the docstring. The PR hasn't been merged: merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}